// aug17d ryouko divergence_000000 (2026-08-18): `type A = B; type B =
// A` was ACCEPTED, and a binding annotated with the cycle typechecked
// against everything — contains' coinductive ref-pair memo seeds
// (ref, T) = true before recursing, and a bare alias cycle closes the
// loop with no structure ever compared, so the hypothesis is the whole
// answer. The absorbed element then rode a heterogeneous array into
// `array::filter(a, |x| x > i64:3)` where the engines' degenerate
// behaviors split: interp kept every element, jit dropped every
// element. Fixed at the def site: `Env::deftype` walks bare-Ref
// bodies via `resolve_pure` (never fills resolution cells) and
// rejects the def that closes a cycle — "circular type alias".
// Recursion through a structural body (variant, union, tuple, ...)
// is untouched; the program is now a CompileErr on both engines.
{type A = B; type B = A; let t: A = f64:0.; {let a = [true, true, t, true, true, true, true, true]; array::filter(a, |x| x > i64:3)}}
